<title>SINGAPORE: Visa International to launch cash card in Tokyo.</title>
<headline>Visa International to launch cash card in Tokyo.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Visa International said on Tuesday it planned to launch a Visa Cash card pilot programme in Shibuya, Tokyo in partnership with eight of its Japan members and two retail conglomerates.</p>
<p>It said in a statement more than 100,000 cash cards would be issued by its participating members, including Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi, Fuji Bank, Sumitomo Bank and retailers Tokyu and Seibu beginning in spring 1998.</p>
<p>The stored value card pilot will include reloadable and disposable cash cards and the reloadable Visa Cash function incorporated onto credit and Automated Teller Machine cards.</p>
<p>Visa Cash will be accepted at fast food outlets, stores, cinemas and the Shibuya train station, which is at the centre of the two-kilometre radius pilot area.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
